                <pb facs="0640" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51/346</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kornfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                        1924</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 25.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 510</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise the Department
                    that Mr. James Grant Forbes of Blair &amp; Company, New York, left Teheran on
                    May 19 for America to confer with his company regarding the loan which the
                    Persian Government seeks to obtain in America. Before his departure, Mr. Forbes
                    had a conference with the Prime Minister, Dr. A. C. Millspaugh, Administrator
                    General of Finances, and the Minister of Finance at which it was decided to
                    pledge all of Persia’s revenues as security for this loan.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph S.
                    Kornfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
